{title: 660 - Glory Be to the Father}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #660 • GLORIA PATRI • 7.4.6.8.7.4.4}
{lyricist: Anonymous, second century}
{composer: H. W. Greatorex}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 660}
{meta: tune GLORIA PATRI}
{meta: meter 7.4.6.8.7.4.4}
{meta: category Sentences and Responses - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb/G]Glory be to the [Ab]Father,
[Fm]and [Bb/F]to [Gm/Bb]the [Bb]Son,
[Bb]and to [Am]the [Bb]Holy Ghost;
[Gm]As [Eb]it [Ab]was [Bb/F]in [Fm]the beginning,
[Bb7]is now, [Eb/Bb]and [Bb]ever shall be,
[Eb/Bb]world without [Ab]end.
[Cm/G]A-men, A--men.
{end_of_verse}
